{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Search & papers analysis — ",
    {{ project_id | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Generated by `llmexer analysis init`.\n",
    "\n",
    "| | |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| project | `",
    {{ project_id | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "| llmexer version | `",
    {{ package_version | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "| generated | `",
    {{ generated_at | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "\n",
    "The cells below only configure paths, call functions and show results.\n",
    "All logic lives in `transform.py`, `stats.py` and `plots.py` next to this\n",
    "notebook.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Folders\n",
    "\n",
    "The next cell derives these from `PROJECT_DIR`:\n",
    "\n",
    "| variable | path |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `DIR_SEARCHES` | `<project>/searches` |\n| `DIR_PAPERS` | `<project>/papers` |\n| `SEARCHES` | `the searches found in the project` |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Change them by hand** if your project is laid out differently — point any of\n",
    "these at an absolute path and re-run the cell, the rest of the notebook follows.\n",
    "\n",
    "`SEARCHES` lists the searches found when this notebook was created — one entry\n",
    "per search, holding its YAML and the `results` / `filter` CSVs written from it\n",
    "(`None` when that file does not exist). It does **not** update itself: add an\n",
    "entry by hand after a new `search run`, or re-scaffold with `--rewrite`.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook analyses **one** search at a time — `SEARCH_INDEX` picks which.\n",
    "Two searches are two different queries, so combining their rows would give\n",
    "year histograms and open-access shares that describe no actual search.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- folders ---------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# This notebook lives in <project>/analysis/, next to the project's other\n",
    "# folders. Edit the paths below if your layout differs.\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "ANALYSIS_DIR = Path.cwd()\n",
    "PROJECT_DIR = ANALYSIS_DIR.parent\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- data folders ----------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "DIR_SEARCHES = PROJECT_DIR / 'searches'\n",
    "DIR_PAPERS = PROJECT_DIR / 'papers'\n",
    "PROJECT_ID = ",
    {{ project_id | tojson | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# One entry per search found when this notebook was scaffolded:\n",
    "# the YAML that defines it, and the CSVs written from it (None if absent).\n",
    "SEARCHES = ",
    {{ searches | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# This notebook analyses ONE search, not all of them combined: results from\n",
    "# different queries are different populations and averaging them says nothing.\n",
    "# Change the index to analyse another search from the list above.\n",
    "SEARCH_INDEX = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- imports ---------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# `transform`, `stats` and `plots` are the copies sitting next to this notebook.\n",
    "if str(ANALYSIS_DIR) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(ANALYSIS_DIR))\n",
    "\n",
    "%matplotlib inline\n",
    "%load_ext autoreload\n",
    "%autoreload 2\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "from plots import plot_results_by_search_engine, setup_style\n",
    "from transform import list_papers, load_search_frame\n",
    "\n",
    "setup_style()\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.max_colwidth', 120)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'project      : {PROJECT_ID}')\n",
    "print(f'analysis dir : {ANALYSIS_DIR}')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load one search and the papers\n",
    "\n",
    "`kind` picks which CSV of the search to read: `results` as it came back, or\n",
    "`filter` for what survived `llmexer search filter`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SEARCH = SEARCHES[SEARCH_INDEX] if SEARCHES else None\n",
    "SEARCH_NAME = SEARCH['search'] if SEARCH else None\n",
    "searches = load_search_frame(DIR_SEARCHES, SEARCH, kind='results')\n",
    "papers = list_papers(DIR_PAPERS)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'search      : {SEARCH_NAME}')\n",
    "print(f'search rows : {len(searches)}')\n",
    "print(f'papers      : {len(papers)}')\n",
    "searches.head()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Results per search engine\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "searches['entry_source'].value_counts().rename('results').to_frame()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Publications per year\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "searches['year'].value_counts().sort_index(ascending=False).rename('publications').to_frame()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Open access and language\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pd.concat(\n",
    "    [\n",
    "        searches['isOpenAccess'].value_counts().rename('open access'),\n",
    "        searches['language'].value_counts().rename('language'),\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    axis=1,\n",
    ")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Papers on disk\n",
    "\n",
    "One row per document stem, with the extractions found next to each PDF.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "papers.agg({'pdf': 'sum', 'txt': 'sum', 'markdown': 'sum', 'extracted': 'sum'}).to_frame('count')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Charts\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plot_results_by_search_engine(searches);\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
